  "posted_text": "🏢 NJ S3379 — Data Centers Must Report Water, Energy Use to NJ\n\nNew Jersey is asking data centers to be more transparent about how they use water and energy. Starting six months after this law takes effect, data center owners and operators must submit semi-annual reports to the Board of Public Utilities. These reports will detail energy consumption, water usage, and how much renewable energy is used – including specific measurements like average air temperatures and waste heat temperatures. ...\n...",
